For the Minimization, I used the Insane script to build my bilayer + pfda system, then I added 6 NA.


Building the Bilayer system with Insane:

insane -o systemdat.gro -l pf10c:1 -l DOPC:99 -sol W -salt 0 -x 20 -y 10 -z 10 -p topol.top

-l specifies which phospholipid to add to the membrane. -sol specifies the solvent. -salt specifies whether or not to add NA and CL ions; if the parameter is 0, then ions will be added to make the system neutral, whereas a positive number will indicate molarity. For example, -salt 0.15 will add NA and CL atoms to set the salt concentration = 0.15.


Adding 1 NA:

For some reason, using -salt 0 in the insane command does not neutralize the -1 charge on the pfda. So I manually added one sodium, NA, ion to the system.

gmx grompp -f inputs/min_strict_steep.mdp -c systemdat.gro -p topology/topol.top -o ions.tpr 
gmx genion -s ions.tpr -p topology/topol.top -pname NA -np 6 -o finalsystem.gro

After adding 6 NA, we now have our final system, with pfda, DOPC, W, and NA. I now did an energy minimization using the mdp files min_strict_steep.mdp and min_strict_cg.mdp

Minimization Part 1 (steepest descent):

gmx grompp -f inputs/min_strict_steep.mdp -c finalsystem.gro -p topology/topol.top -o minimized_steep.tpr 
gmx mdrun -s minimized_steep.tpr -v -deffnm minimized_steep

Minimization Part 2 (Conjugate Gradient descent):

gmx grompp -f inputs/min_strict_cg.mdp -c minimized_steep.gro -p topology/topol.top -o minimized_cg.tpr
gmx mdrun -s minimized_cg.tpr -v -deffnm minimized_cg
